      "description": "Watch PAOK vs Anderlecht highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 6, 2026. The atmosphere in the UEFA Europa League was thick with anticipation as both teams took to the pitch. Held on August 6, 2026 , this fixture promised an intense tactical battle between two sides eager to assert their dominance in the competition. An Electric Start The match exploded into life within the first minute as PAOK took the lead. Mihajlo Cvetkovic found the back of the net, capitalizing on a clinical assist from Enric Llansana . This early blow left Anderlecht reeling, forcing the visitors to scramble and adjust their defensive setup against the sustained pressure of the home side. Tension and Missed Chances Despite their early success, PAOK could not capitalize on their momentum to put the game to bed. In the 35th minute, Giannis Michailidis stepped up for a penalty, but he failed to convert the opportunity. This miss gave Anderlecht a lifeline, and the game quickly grew more aggressive. Before the half-time whistle, Pantelis Hatzidiakos was cautioned as the referee began to pull out cards to keep control of the rising intensity. Tactical Shifts and Late Discipline The second half saw a flurry of substitutions as both managers looked for fresh legs, with Aritz Elustondo replacing Hatzidiakos , and players like Dimitrios Pelkas entering the fray. As the clock ticked down, the discipline of the match deteriorated, with Moussa N'Diaye , Enric Llansana , Aritz Elustondo , and Danylo Sikan all picking up yellow cards. Despite the late drama and physical challenges, the referee brought the match to a close after five minutes of added time."
